<h1>draw — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="sub">Last updated 20 August 2026</p>

<p><strong>draw</strong> is a diagramming tool operated by apnex (<code>apnex.com.au</code>) at
<code>draw.apnex.io</code>. It is a single-operator tool, not a commercial service, and has no
user accounts of its own.</p>

<h2>What is collected</h2>

<p><strong>Your Google account email, for access control only.</strong> Access is gated by Google
Cloud Identity-Aware Proxy (IAP). IAP verifies your Google identity before any request reaches the
application. The application itself does not read, store or log your email address; authorisation is
enforced entirely by Google Cloud IAM.</p>

<p><strong>Diagram content.</strong> Diagrams you create are stored as JSON in Google Cloud Storage.
This includes node names, labels, and any text you type into a diagram. Please do not put
confidential information into a diagram.</p>

<p><strong>Google Slides access, only if you choose to connect it.</strong> Connecting Google Slides
grants the <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/presentations</code> scope, which permits creating
and modifying Google Slides presentations in your account. It is used solely to push a diagram you
explicitly choose, to a presentation you explicitly nominate. The resulting OAuth token is held
server-side and used for nothing else.</p>

<h2>What is not collected</h2>

<p>No analytics, tracking, advertising, profiling or telemetry of any kind. The application sets no
cookies of its own; IAP sets a session cookie in order to authenticate you. No data is sold, shared
or disclosed to third parties.</p>

<h2>Where data is held</h2>

<p>Google Cloud Platform, in the <code>australia-southeast1</code> region. Diagram data lives in a
private Cloud Storage bucket with public access prevention enforced, readable and writable only by
the application's own service account.</p>

<h2>Retention and deletion</h2>

<p>Diagrams persist until you delete them. Deleting a diagram in the application removes the stored
object, and deleting every diagram removes all diagram data held for you.</p>

<p>Google Slides access can be revoked at any time, independently of this application, at
<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>. Revoking it
stops all further access to your presentations.</p>

<h2>Enquiries</h2>

<p>Enquiries about this policy should be directed to the support contact shown on the Google consent
screen presented when you sign in to this application.</p>

<footer>This page is served from a public bucket, separate from the application, so that it remains
reachable without signing in.</footer>
